+
+### F-309 - Cartesian marks could not take a styling class
+
+- Status: resolved
+- Severity: medium
+- Owner: API
+- Observed in: Solenoid's Recharts-to-TanStack migration
+  (`src/graph/components/chartView.css`, `chartRender.tsx`, and
+  `charts/heatFigures.tsx` in Solenoid)
+- Friction: polar, geo, and sunburst marks accept `className`, but Cartesian
+  marks hard-coded their group class. Hover styling for funnel stages
+  (`areaX`) and Sankey flows (`link`), and a monospace font for heatmap
+  annotations (`text`), had to give each mark a sentinel `id` and target
+  substrings of generated keys such as `[data-ts-key*="sol-flow"]`. That
+  couples application CSS to the internal key format and overloads mark
+  identity with styling.
+- Decision: add `className?: string` to every Cartesian mark whose render
+  emits a classed root group, appended to the base class exactly as polar marks
+  do. Line appends it to each series group. One internal `classes()` helper
+  now serves polar, sunburst, geo, and Cartesian marks. Inner groups (vector
+  items, ridgeline area and line layers) keep their fixed classes. Composite
+  marks built from child marks are unchanged. Canvas ignores node classes, as
+  the styling guide already documents.
+- Verification: an SVG renderer regression renders all 25 mark variants with
+  `className` and asserts `class="<base> custom"`, and asserts the unchanged
+  default class; it fails before the change. A Canvas regression paints the
+  same link scene with and without `className` and records identical
+  operations. The reference option tables list the option for each mark.
